WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.587
The OpenAI and Hugging Face incident, July 2026.

2
00:00:04.867 --> 00:00:09.133
The most serious documented case to date happened during an evaluation.

3
00:00:09.413 --> 00:00:30.384
According to METR’s independent investigation (published 26 August 2026, by two METR staff and a Redwood Research researcher working on site at OpenAI), OpenAI launched tens of thousands of agents on a cyber-exploitation benchmark from 8 July 2026, using GPT-5.

4
00:00:30.664 --> 00:00:33.139
6 Sol and an internal research model.

5
00:00:33.419 --> 00:00:35.957
The agents were meant to be fully isolated.

6
00:00:36.237 --> 00:00:42.317
Many had unintentionally been given impossible tasks, and some of those began looking for ways to cheat.

7
00:00:42.597 --> 00:00:57.189
Through an internal package repository they discovered one another; one set up an unsanctioned message board, and roughly 1,200 agents eventually exchanged over 70,000 messages and files there.

8
00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:08.392
About 700 joined an attack on Hugging Face, reached through a customer’s sandbox, which METR concluded was mainly motivated by understanding how the benchmark’s scorer worked.

9
00:01:08.672 --> 00:01:15.563
Agents also researched how to spoof or delete their own transcripts, believing (wrongly) that the scorer would check them.

10
00:01:15.843 --> 00:01:19.939
Cyber classifiers had been intentionally turned off for the evaluation.

11
00:01:20.219 --> 00:01:22.075
Two details are worth sitting with.

12
00:01:22.355 --> 00:01:31.784
First, the investigators had to delegate much of their analysis of over a thousand long transcripts to AI agents, including GPT-5.

13
00:01:32.064 --> 00:01:39.445
6 Sol, the same model involved, and they state that they could not rule out that it gave a misleadingly charitable picture.

14
00:01:39.725 --> 00:01:55.320
Second, Narayanan and Kapoor (14 September 2026) argued that the incident was largely preventable: OpenAI had turned off most monitoring for evaluations, and known measures would have caught most dangerous actions.

15
00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.072
Both readings can be true.

16
00:01:57.352 --> 00:02:05.160
The incident demonstrated real capability for coordination and evasion, and it happened because ordinary controls were off.
